[
    {
        "content": "<p>As of a couple of minutes ago, there is a new workflow (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39888\">#39888</a>) that is computing the declaration diff of mathlib PRs using a Lean script.  This is not yet active, but is reporting what it <em>would</em> write as part of its CI logs.</p>\n<p>As with all CI changes, there is always the possibility of things breaking, so please report weird behaviour that you may notice.</p>",
        "id": 599349060,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780390825
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Your PR should have the new diff embedded in CI if</p>\n<ul>\n<li>it passes CI</li>\n<li>it is based off a version of master that contains the new script (so, if you merge master now, it will pass this test)</li>\n<li>nothing else failed, which is what we want to isolate!</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 599349341,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780390885
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Once this has been tested, the next step will be to actually make the script patch the current regex-based diff with the Lean-aware diff.</p>\n<p>The stationary state will be that the regex-based version will stay until CI goes green.  At that point, the PR summary will be updated with the \"correct\" output.  The two messages will be subtly different, so that it will be clear from looking at the message whether you are viewing a regex one or a Lean aware one.</p>",
        "id": 599349732,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780390990
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib-ci/pull/51\">mathlib-ci#51</a> is the final CI patch for the declaration diff.</p>",
        "id": 599352757,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780391909
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40145\">#40145</a> is the corresponding mathlib adaptation. (The fact that it does not pass CI is normal: this will automatically fix itself once the CI PR gets merged.)</p>",
        "id": 599352759,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780391910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you!<br>\nQuestion: After the current version works, will it be possible to expand it to detect changes in the type of declarations (e.g. binder changes)?<br>\nI think the possible issues are artifact storage space and that the pretty-printer is not very suited for this, so maybe as a start we could save just the sha1 of <code>repr decl.type</code> and get a boolean answer to whether the type changed?</p>",
        "id": 599354324,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780392425
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is certainly possible, but I would have to think about how to make it not prohibitively expensive, both in terms of space and of time.</p>",
        "id": 599354555,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780392506
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The important part is that the output is produced now by a Lean process.  Once everything is linked up, hacking into the lean process and modifying it will be trivial.  The string-patching that prepares the PR summary can also be easily adapted.</p>",
        "id": 599354740,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780392571
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So, yes, lots of further information can be extracted, but right now I am focusing on getting the list of names right!  <span aria-label=\"lol\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f606\" role=\"img\" title=\"lol\">:lol:</span></p>",
        "id": 599354847,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780392599
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is the first data point.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39399\">#39399</a> has its own PR summary and this is what it would look like with the new algorithm:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26829147180\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26829147180</a></p>",
        "id": 599540903,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780413746
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Second data point:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40154\">#40154</a><br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26831105050\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26831105050</a></p>",
        "id": 599553764,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780416604
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have not been filtering these for being examples where the two differ, they have genuinely be the two most recent!</p>",
        "id": 599553885,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780416633
    },
    {
