 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26842066868\">26842066868</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38142\">#38142</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+6 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+2 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26841567290\">26841567290</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40161\">#40161</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26841395376\">26841395376</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38612\">#38612</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+16 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+8 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26841309567\">26841309567</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40106\">#40106</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+15 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+6 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26840352392\">26840352392</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40160\">#40160</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26840040553\">26840040553</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36165\">#36165</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26839672327\">26839672327</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40159\">#40159</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26839098818\">26839098818</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40127\">#40127</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26838987973\">26838987973</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39890\">#39890</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+12 / −1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26836115704\">26836115704</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/32983\">#32983</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+42 / −46</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+19 / −35</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26835509134\">26835509134</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40134\">#40134</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+1 / −1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26835194315\">26835194315</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40157\">#40157</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26834821619\">26834821619</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40155\">#40155</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+35 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+25 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26834541245\">26834541245</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40153\">#40153</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26834462061\">26834462061</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40101\">#40101</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+3 / −2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+3 / −2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26834047080\">26834047080</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38669\">#38669</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+15 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+15 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26833917133\">26833917133</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38214\">#38214</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+16 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+21 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26833291926\">26833291926</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36541\">#36541</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+168 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+34 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26832472081\">26832472081</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39357\">#39357</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+100 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+80 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26832108748\">26832108748</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40032\">#40032</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+8 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+2 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26831391172\">26831391172</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40154\">#40154</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+0 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26831308641\">26831308641</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35136\">#35136</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+37 / −2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+27 / −1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26831281063\">26831281063</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38698\">#38698</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+7 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+7 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26829667999\">26829667999</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40044\">#40044</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+2 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+2 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/actions/runs/26829147180\">26829147180</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39399\">#39399</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+42 / −0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">+19 / −0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
        "id": 599709690,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780470731
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Besides the obvious (<code>to_additive</code> and friends, <code>instance</code>s), the main source of differences are</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>.casesOn</code>, <code>.mk</code> and other autogenerated declarations appear in the Lean-aware</li>\n<li><code>private</code> declarations <em>do not</em> appear in the Lean-aware!  (I probably simply need to add <code>import all</code> somewhere)</li>\n<li><code>simps</code>-generated declarations (<del>maybe they should be removed from the diff?</del> See Michael's comment below)</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 599710226,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780470897
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you spot anything else or have some comments, please, let me know.  Currently, I think that the regex-based version is not fully replaced by the Lean-aware version, but I would like it to be so that all the information contained in the regex version is also available in the Lean-aware one.</p>",
        "id": 599710702,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780471030
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think changes in <code>simps</code>-generated declarations are important: if, for instance, I make simps auto-generated previously manually written declarations, I would like the diff to pick that up. (Similarly when renaming the declarations simps generates, etc.)</p>",
        "id": 599718669,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1780473154
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Good point, thanks!</p>",
        "id": 599719317,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780473312
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, thinking about wanting them to show up in the diff: if you remove a <code>simps</code> and manually create declarations with the same name, that would <em>not</em> show up in the Lean-aware diff, but would have showed up in the regex based one.</p>",
        "id": 599720103,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780473497
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is maybe a good way of framing the two diffs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the regex-based one is a weak approximation to a <code>Syntax</code>-aware diff</li>\n<li>the Lean-aware diff is an (exact?) diff of the names of the constants that exist in the final environment</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 599720647,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780473612
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder whether maybe we should also promote the regex-based diff to an actual Syntactic diff and then keep both.</p>",
        "id": 599721056,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780473703
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This looks great!</p>\n<p>One question. Does this also work for toolchain bump PR? I have seen toolchain bump PR accidentally dropping a theorem twice (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39980#issuecomment-4614988642\">example</a>). There is no way for human to review a +9035 change across 2.5k files, so I hope this tool can catch and print such diff?</p>",
        "id": 599887107,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1780512236
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It should, since it does not really \"compare\" environments, it simply stores to a file all the declarations in the two environments and then basically computes the diff of the two lists.</p>",
        "id": 599888064,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780512476
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>However, note that the example that you linked also has some <code>-</code> in the current declaration diff that are not clearly paired with some <code>+</code>, so human inspection is still going to be needed.</p>",
        "id": 599888470,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780512577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The new Lean-aware declarations diff is part of CI for every PR that targets recent master and passes CI!</p>\n<p>Since I do not think that this Lean-aware diff is fully capable yet of replacing the old, regex-based one, in this transition period both reports coexist.  The original one appears shortly after the PR is opened, as it currently does.</p>\n<p>The Lean-aware one gets triggered by successfully passing <code>lake build</code> and updates a second diff, visible in the PR summary comment.</p>\n<p>The Lean-aware tab has 3 stages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pending</code> meaning that the CI steps are not done yet</li>\n<li><code>unavailable</code> signaling that something went wrong -- either just merging master it is enough to make it go away, or some internal error of the script (please report these!)</li>\n<li>message present -- the happy place!</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 600103682,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780583635
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40225\">#40225</a> may be the first PR to receive the new report.</p>",
        "id": 600113217,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780586016
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(It still does not show the <code>private</code> declarations, since I have not actually acted on the list above, I was just collecting future issues, while testing that the whole setup works.)</p>",
        "id": 600113389,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780586060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am curious in some technical detail. How does the script determine the \"base version\" and \"new version\"? A few options that I can think of all have some problem:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Latest master vs PR latest commit: would it show diff of dropping theorems from diverged master?</li>\n<li>Latest master vs {Latest master merged with PR}: Does CI need to build the merged version separately?</li>\n<li>{Divergent point between master and PR} vs PR latest commit: Would a merge-from-master in the PR break this?</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 600123378,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1780588807
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The script uses the merge-base with master as the \"base\" commit and the head of the PR as the \"new\" version.</p>",
        "id": 600123639,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780588878
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It needs to have the file with the declarations on both, so it needs to target a master commit that has passed CI.</p>",
        "id": 600123744,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780588909
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And it waits until that step has been built on the PR before it computes the diff.</p>",
        "id": 600123794,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780588923
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the explanation!</p>",
        "id": 600124566,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1780589127
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Btw, the actual diff is really a text-based diff on Lean-extracted declaration names.  This part can be extended: the Lean script that reports the declaration names could report more, the script that reads the files could do more sophisticated analysis.</p>",
        "id": 600124607,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1780589139
    }
]